! AlwaysOn: EnergyPlus needs a schedule where the xlsx gives none: for loads whose schedule in the prototype is constant 1, and for the operating mode of the heat pump fans (the xlsx dictionary says constant volume fan control: the fan runs continuously).
  Schedule:Compact,
    AlwaysOn,                     !- Name
    ,                             !- Schedule Type Limits Name
    Through: 12/31,               !- Field 1
    For: AllDays,                 !- Field 2
    Until: 24:00,                 !- Field 3
    1;                            !- Field 4

  Schedule:Compact,
    ACTIVITY_SCH,                 !- Name  Not in the documents: the prototype value 95 (the PDF has no schedule table for the high-rise apartment); EnergyPlus needs an activity level for People.
    ,                             !- Schedule Type Limits Name
    Through: 12/31,               !- Field 1
    For: AllDays,                 !- Field 2
    Until: 24:00,95;              !- Field 3

! Thermostats: the xlsx gives a heating and a cooling set point schedule for the apartments and one for the office (sheet Schedule Summary); a zone uses the schedules of its set point control in the prototype, checked against the xlsx hourly values.
  HVACTemplate:Thermostat,
    ApartmentThermostat1,         !- Name
    HTGSETP_APT_SCH,              !- Heating Setpoint Schedule Name  Source: xlsx Schedule Summary 'Heating Set Point', rows 767/768/769 (Mon - Fri/Sat/Sun).
    ,                             !- Constant Heating Setpoint
    CLGSETP_APT_SCH;              !- Cooling Setpoint Schedule Name  Source: xlsx Schedule Summary 'Cooling Set Point', rows 761/762/763 (Mon - Fri/Sat/Sun).

  HVACTemplate:Zone:WaterToAirHeatPump,
    G SW Apartment,               !- Zone Name  Source: xlsx raw_data!I2 HVAC System Name = AIRLOOP G SW. xlsx HVAC System Type 15.
